GreyEnergy and CrashOverride share similarities in their objectives as they both aim to cause significant disruptions in industrial control systems (ICS). However, GreyEnergy is more versatile in its approach, exhibiting capabilities for espionage, data exfiltration, and sabotage, while CrashOverride is primarily designed for destructive purposes, focusing on disabling ICS functionality to cause physical damage.
